<p:notes xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:p="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/presentationml/2006/main"><p:cSld><p:spTree><p:nvGrpSpPr><p:cNvPr id="1" name=""><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{B7EF7ED2-7C84-1C83-6533-DB0AD5C840E3}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvGrpSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvGrpSpPr><p:grpSpPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="0" cy="0"/><a:chOff x="0" y="0"/><a:chExt cx="0" cy="0"/></a:xfrm></p:grpSpPr><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="2" name="Slide Image Placeholder 1"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{D23066AF-9502-0E4E-66DE-5B77490BBEB5}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1" noRot="1" noChangeAspect="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="sldImg"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr/></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="3" name="Notes Placeholder 2"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{CE461928-F6B9-2F7A-BC4F-EF76E1E26136}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="body" idx="1"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr/><p:txBody><a:bodyPr/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>DELIVERY</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>About one minute. One example per box.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>SPEAKER NARRATION</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>Most machine-learning problems fall into a handful of task types, and the task is defined by the kind of answer you want back. Classification answers 'which category?': fraud or not fraud, spam or not spam. Regression answers 'what number?': the sale price of a home, which ties back to our structured-data example. Clustering answers 'what groups exist?' without labels, which is the unsupervised learning we just saw. Anomaly detection answers 'what looks unusual?': an odd transaction or a sensor reading that doesn't fit.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>The task tells you what you need. Many different algorithms can do each one, and choosing among them is the data scientist's job.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>TRANSITION</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr dirty="0"/><a:t>Next: deep learning.</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="4" name="Slide Number Placeholder 3"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{49AD4375-339A-7880-6F76-FFCA173EBD7A}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="sldNum" sz="quarter" idx="10"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr/><p:txBody><a:bodyPr/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:fld id="{18D02FFD-07D4-5C4F-BD77-921008177348}" type="slidenum"><a:rPr lang="en-US" smtClean="0"/><a:t>23</a:t></a:fld><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp></p:spTree><p:extLst><p:ext uri="{BB962C8B-B14F-4D97-AF65-F5344CB8AC3E}"><p14:creationId xmlns:p14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/powerpoint/2010/main" val="517432880"/></p:ext></p:extLst></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:notes>